s likely that apple will  switch to this  new wired magsafe connector before they  would go  fully portless since this connector will  be able to transfer  data while improving convenience and  water resistance  now whether or not this happens for the  iphone 13 pro max this year  i'm not sure but we did also have a  rumor from john prosser  saying that we will have at least one  portless iphone model  in 2021 but either way i'm very  confident that we will be seeing  this new magnetic port coming to the  iphone 14 lineup in 2022  basically making it portless since a  connector is technically  not a port now moving on we have a very  interesting  and kind of hard to believe leak from  inchikwo he says that at least  the high-end 2022 iphones will be  getting a  hole punch display design similar to a  lot of the higher-end samsung phones  like the s21 ultra now this is a bit  hard to believe  because apple would have to figure out a  way to move the face  id sensors and components away from the  display area  to get rid of the notch since we're  pretty sure apple will continue to use  face id  for many many years now since most of  the iphone 13 leaks  show that the speaker grille is being  moved to the top literally right next to  the frame  i personally believe that the best way  for apple to do this  is to split the sensors apart and fit  them on both sides of the speaker grille  allowing for a nice and thin bezel and  then on top of that  quo mentioned that he expects at least  one iphone in 2023  to have a full screen display with no  notch  and no holes which is the dream now a  couple of months back  digitimes claimed that the lighter  scanner that we currently have  on the iphone 12 pro models will be  expanding to the entire iphone 13  lineup but i find that hard to believe  because lidar just came out  with the 12 pro and recent leaks are  also pointing to the less expensive 13  models  not getting lidar as you can see in this  leaked  cad image but based on that i fully  expect the entire iphone 14 lineup  to get lidar in 2022 so that's  definitely something to look forward to  now moving on we're basically 100 sure  that the iphone 13 pro models  this year will be getting 120 hertz  refresh rate on the displays  and because of that there are some  people expecting the entire iphone 14  lineup next year  getting 120 hertz but in my opinion i  don't see that happening until at least  2023  the reason for that is because apple  first released promotion 120 hertz  back in 2017 for the 10.5 inch ipad pro  and now almost four years later the only  apple product with 120 hertz is the ipad  pro  not even the new ipad air that was just  released a few months ago  so because of that it seems like apple  wants to keep the high refresh rate a  pro exclusive feature  at least for now so i expect apple to  only give it to the low end iphones in  2023 at least just to make the pros feel  more exclusive and at that point the  pros will probably have 240hz refresh  rate  since apple actually won a patent for an  iphone display with variable refresh  rate  up to 240hz now the same thing goes for  another leak from digitimes  claiming that every iphone 13 model will  be getting  sensor shift stabilization this year i  once again think that just the iphone 13  pros  are gonna have this feature including  the smaller model  and then next year it's gonna come down  to every iphone 14 model  and on top of that since tsmc's three  nanometer chips are expected to hit  volume production  in 2022 we can for sure expect powerful  3 nanometer a15 chips in the iphone 14  lineup but now  let's get into the very juicy leaks that  prove that the 2022 iphones  are going to be absolutely game-changing  ming chi ko says that the iphone 14 pro  models will get a  48 megapixel main camera that's capable  of shooting  8k video now this is a huge deal because  for the past  five years iphones have been strictly  limited to a 12 megapixel main camera  even the brand new 12 pro max and even  better  quo says that apple will use pixel  binning to merge the 48 megapixel output  down into a 12 megapixel photo which  will essentially make the pixel size  a massive 2.5 micrometers larger than  what  any smartphone can do bringing it close  to professional camera quality  for low light imagery this in the new 8k  video recording feature will essentially  bring smartphone photography to a whole  new level  and it would basically bring ak video to  the mainstream  since the industry usually follows in  apple's footsteps  now on top of that ming also mentioned  that the 5.4 inch iphone mini size  will be discontinued in 2022  and that's of course due to the very low  sales numbers  that the current 12 mini has which  ultimately led to us making this review  showing off why it failed now with that  if apple's getting rid of the mini size  then what are they going to replace it  with well apparently makeshift says that  there will actually be  two large 6.7 inch iphone 14 models next  year a  low end model and a high-end pro model  which is really really weird i  personally have a hard time believing  this because currently  the people who want a large display have  to pay extra for the pro max model  and that means extra revenue for apple  but with what quo is saying people can  get a large display  for a cheaper price so because of that i  have a totally  different theory what if the second 6.7  inch iphone  is actually a foldable iphone  now i know that sounds crazy but let me  explain we've been getting leaks about  apple's foldable phone for months or  even years now  with everything ranging from patents for  the hinge system to even  sending foldable phones to foxconn for  durability testing  and these leaks started way back in 2017  especially with this patent image of a  foldable iphone  with a flexible display but then on the  other hand  they also applied for patents for a  larger ipad mini like display  with two separate panels instead of a  flexible panel  so here's my theory what if apple is  actually working on  two foldable iphones and the first one  that's been rumored to be coming in 2022  will have a flexible 6.7 inch display  that folds vertically like a flip phone  like you see in this image and this  could totally go in line with a report  from the verifier last year  claiming that a new foldable iphone is  coming in 2022  for 1500 which actually seems like a  reasonable price  this makes total sense because last year  it was reported  that two different foldable iphone  prototypes passed  internal durability testing so i did a  little digging and i found that john  prosser is thinking along the same lines  as i am  but obviously before i realize this one  flip phone style foldable  and one larger foldable so i personally  believe  that next year apple is going to release  a 6.7 inch iphone  flip with a flexible display for around  fifteen hundred dollars  and then in the future maybe 2023 or 24  they'll release the larger foldable that  has two separate panels  so yeah i told you that next year is  gonna be  world changing for apple but beyond that  manchester is also expecting an iphone  se3 model  coming in the first half of 2022 but it  looks like it's going to maintain  the same 4.7 inch display for at least  another year and apparently  ross young believes we'll be getting a  fully redesigned  se model in 2023 with a 6.1 inch display  and a hole punch camera instead of a  notch so there you guys go  that's basically everything you should  expect in terms of 2022 and future  iphones  and i've got to say it's going to be an  absolutely killer year for apple  because they're going to be changing the  smartphone camera game  with the new 48 megapixel camera and  they'll basically make foldable phones  mainstream  by releasing the iphone flip so  hopefully you guys enjoy this video and  if you disagree with anything that i  said  leave a comment down below but if you 